TSycRFIDReader - Sycreader USB RFID reader (keyboard emulator) as a chip card
reader of the PascalSCADA security system.

LINUX (and probably FreeBSD/macOS)
  - Reads the reader through libhidapi (hidapi-libusb), so this package adds a
    static link to libhidapi. Install it first or you will get a non working
    Lazarus install. On Debian, Ubuntu, Mint and derivatives:
      sudo apt install libhidapi-dev
  - Install 99-zzzrfid.rules in /etc/udev/rules.d. It unbinds the reader from
    the kernel keyboard driver (so the codes aren't typed in the focused
    window) and gives access to the device.
  - Only tested on Linux.

WINDOWS
  - No external library nor driver is needed. Windows doesn't allow libhidapi
    to read HID keyboards, so the codes are taken with the Raw Input API, only
    from the device that matches VendorID/ProductID (and SerialNumber, if set).
  - While the component is active, the keystrokes of the reader are dropped
    before they reach the controls of the application (keyboard hook of the
    main thread). Other applications in foreground still receive them, as
    Windows doesn't allow to stop them without a system wide hook.
  - The component must be created and used on the main thread.
